The following opcodes have costs below:

In this table, <code>signature_work(signature)</code> is <code>HASH(96) + SIGCHECK</code> for a nonempty signature and zero for an empty one.  <code>HASH(96)</code> is BIP 340's challenge hash over the 96 bytes <code><nowiki>R || P || m</nowiki></code>.  This rule also applies to unknown nonzero-length public-key types.

{|
! Opcode
! Varops Budget Cost
|-
|OP_CHECKLOCKTIMEVERIFY
|BASE + READ(length(operand))
|-
|OP_CHECKSEQUENCEVERIFY
|BASE + READ(length(operand))
|-
|OP_CHECKSIGADD
|BASE + READ(length(number operand)) + signature_work(signature) + (if signature is nonempty: ARITH(length(number operand)); otherwise 0) + WRITE(length(result))
|-
|OP_CHECKSIG
|BASE + signature_work(signature) + WRITE(length(result))
|-
|OP_CHECKSIGVERIFY
|BASE + signature_work(signature)
