OP_CHECKSIGADD always reads its numeric operand and writes its numeric result.  Its increment traversal and signature work are charged only for a nonempty signature.

===Other Operators===

The varops costs of the other existing opcodes are defined in [[bip-0440.mediawiki|BIP440]].  Any opcode not costed there or in this document costs only BASE, unless another BIP specifies a charge.

==Security Considerations==

The 8,000,000-byte stack limit counts logical lengths, not allocated capacity, so an implementation that keeps a shortened value in its former buffer can grow memory through repeated duplication and truncation.  The reference implementation copies a shortened value into a right-sized buffer when the value's capacity exceeds twice its word span, which bounds stack storage to about twice the logical limit.  Each such copy is at most half the size of the buffer it replaces, so a chain of copies starting from one buffer totals at most that buffer's size, which the <code>WRITE</code> that produced its value, or the value's weight as a witness item, paid for.  Implementations must also bound temporary storage and concurrent evaluations.  Memory usage never affects script validity.

==Backwards compatibility==

This BIP defines a previously unused (and thus, always-successful) tapscript
version, for backwards compatibility.

